/-!
# The coherent reflexive hull

Source: Stacks Project, Divisors, Tag 0AY4 (lemma-dual-reflexive), the observation after
the definition of reflexive hull preceding Tag 0AY0, and remark-tensor;
More on Algebra, Tag 0AV3 (blueprint: lem-sfb-coherent-reflexive-hull).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules

/-- The double internal dual of a coherent module on an integral locally Noetherian scheme
is coherent, and its canonical evaluation into its own double dual is an isomorphism.

Source: Stacks Project, Divisors, Tag 0AY4 (lemma-dual-reflexive) and remark-tensor,
and More on Algebra, Tag 0AV3 (blueprint: lem-sfb-coherent-reflexive-hull).

Proof:
1. The structure sheaf is quasi-coherent, since on an affine it is the tilde of the rank-one
free module, and of finite type, generated by 1. Local Noetherianity therefore makes it
coherent (pqf-lem-coherent-ft-locnoeth).
2. For coherent G, internal Hom from G into the structure sheaf is locally a kernel between
finite sums of the structure sheaf (lem-weil-pbc-coherent-hom-local-kernel). Restrictions,
finite sums and kernels of coherent modules are coherent, and coherence is local on an
open cover. Apply this first to H and then to its dual, obtaining coherence of both duals.
3. On a nonempty affine W = Spec A, A is a Noetherian domain. The module P of sections of
H's dual is finite. The affine tilde-Gamma adjunction and its counit identify sections of
Q = H's double dual with Hom_A(P,A), by taking a sheaf morphism to its map on W-sections.
This identification is A-linear and commutes with evaluation.
4. The finite A-module A is reflexive, by identifying Hom_A(A,A) with A via evaluation at 1.
The Hom-into-reflexive theorem over a Noetherian domain
(lem-sfb-finite-hom-reflexive-domain) makes Hom_A(P,A) reflexive. Naturality of evaluation
transports this to Q(W). On the empty affine, all section modules are zero and evaluation
is the unique isomorphism.
5. The affine reflexivity comparison (lem-sfb-affine-reflexive-module-comparison) now makes
the actual sheaf evaluation Q -> Q's double dual an isomorphism. No normality is used. -/
theorem coherent_reflexive_hull (X : Scheme.{u}) [IsIntegral X] [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    (H : X.Modules) (hH : RingedSpace.IsCoherent X.toRingedSpace H) :
    RingedSpace.IsCoherent X.toRingedSpace
      (SheafOfModules.homObj (R := X.sheaf)
        (SheafOfModules.homObj (R := X.sheaf) H (SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf))
        (SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf)) ∧
      IsIso (SheafOfModules.bidual (R := X.sheaf)
        (SheafOfModules.homObj (R := X.sheaf)
          (SheafOfModules.homObj (R := X.sheaf) H (SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf))
          (SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf))) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules
